        "translation_review": "workflows/reviews/missal-english-completion-2026-10-29/roman-1962/translation-review.json",
        "translation_note": "Puerile decus is rendered with its compact image, 'the splendor of childhood,' rather than supplying an unprinted choir or company.",
        "translations": [
          {
            "lang": "en",
            "rights": "project-created",
            "text": "May glory, praise, and honor be yours, Christ the King and Redeemer, to whom the splendor of childhood uttered a devout Hosanna. / You are Israel's King and David's renowned offspring, blessed King, who come in the Lord's name. / The whole heavenly assembly praises you on high, and mortal humanity and all created things together. / The Hebrew people came to meet you with palms; here we stand before you with prayer, vows, and hymns. / They offered you tributes of praise as you were about to suffer; here we sing a song for you as you reign. / They pleased you; may our devotion please you, good King, merciful King, whom all good things please.\n"
          }
        ]
      },
      "replacement": "checked historical English",
      "review": "workflows/reviews/missal-english-completion-2026-10-29/roman-1962/sources/source-review-f76ae4fce9a3a9dd.json"
    },
